   "text": "Geometric sequences"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "What do I need to know about geometric sequences?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- In a **geometric sequence,** there is a **common ratio** between consecutive terms in the sequence"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/06/4.5.1-Geom-Seq-Illustr.png",
   "file": "assets/9fb74f1ac39c-4-5-1-geom-seq-illustr.png",
   "alt": "Geom Seq Illustr, A Level & AS Level Pure Maths Revision Notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- You need to know the ***n***<sup>**th**</sup>** term formula** for a geometric sequence $u_{n}=ar^{n-1}$\n\n  - a is the first term\n  - *r *is the common ratio"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "variant": "exam-tip",
   "label": "Exam Hint",
   "md": "If you know two terms in a geometric sequence you can find ***a*** and ***r*** using simultaneous equations.\n\n![Geom Seq Simult, A Level & AS Level Pure Maths Revision Notes](assets/62f7098d08c1-4-5-1-geom-seq-simult.png)"
  },
